 Add `--json` to get a JSON object instead.
 
+### Caching
+
+Parsing dominates the runtime on large files. Pass `--cache` to store the
+parsed records on disk and reuse them on the next run over the same file:
+
+```
+logslice --cache huge.log --count-by level   # parses and caches
+logslice --cache huge.log --level error      # served from the cache
+```
+
+Cached results are stored as JSON, one entry per log file, in a directory
+resolved in this order: `$LOGSLICE_CACHE_DIR` (used as-is), then
+`$XDG_CACHE_HOME/logslice`, then `~/.cache/logslice`. The cache key includes
+the file's size and modification time, so editing or appending to a log
+invalidates its entry. Entries expire after `--cache-ttl SECONDS` (default
+3600); delete the directory to clear the cache.
+
 ## Development
 
 ```
